Name: glib
URL: https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/glib
Version: 2.90.1
Revision: e05063ccc6c8f222465a1080927f4c14349f3de6
Update Mechanism: Manual (https://crbug.com/503546519)
License: LGPL-2.1
License File: LICENSE
Shipped: no
Security Critical: no

Description:
Low-level core library that forms the basis for projects such as GTK+ and GNOME.

This is only used in tests.

Local Modifications:
None.

Generated code (enum types, D-Bus code, and visibility and version macros) is
generated at build time from the in-tree glib using the codegen wrappers and
templates in this directory (see codegen.gni). Only the headers produced by
meson's host configuration checks are checked in, under include/.

When updating to a new version, update the Revision above with the new commit hash,
and perform the following steps:
1. Add any new sources and generated-code inputs from the upstream meson.build
   files to BUILD.gn.
2. If upstream changed its configuration checks, run on_update.sh and check in
   the regenerated headers under include/.
